.TH start-cli-server-trusted-keys-add 1  "add "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-add \- Import public keys; newly added keys are trusted for packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli server trusted\-keys add\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\-for\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPUBLIC_KEYS\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import public keys; newly added keys are trusted for packages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: ]
Name for the key; blank names each GPG key after its identity
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\-for\fR \fI<TRUST_FOR>\fR
Grant this trust to every imported key, including keys already present
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
marketplace
.IP \(bu 2
os
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPUBLIC_KEYS\fR>
Ed25519 public keys in PEM or armored GPG format; put options before \-\- and keys after it
